  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many patients can the hospital admit per week during the outbreak? Due to the coronavirus outbreak, 55 patients are admitted into the hospital each day. During the outbreak, the hospital's weekly patient-admission report is reviewed by the hospital's administrative office. The report categorizes admitted patients by department, such as emergency medicine, pediatrics, and surgery. The hospital uses an electronic registration system to record each patient's admission date.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "EXACT PUBLIC STATE AFTER TURN 6; NO PRIVATE OR FUTURE DATA\nPUBLIC_STATE_JSON:\n{\"completed_task_turns\":[{\"turn\":1,\"user_message\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nHow many patients can the hospital admit per week during the outbreak? Due to the coronavirus outbreak, 55 patients are admitted into the hospital each day. During the outbreak, the hospital's weekly patient-admission report is reviewed by the hospital's administrative office. The report categorizes admitted patients by department, such as emergency medicine, pediatrics, and surgery. The hospital uses an electronic registration system to record each patient's admission date.\"},{\"turn\":2,\"user_message\":\"Wait, I made a mistake. Due to the coronavirus outbreak, 50 patients are admitted into the hospital each day.\"},{\"turn\":3,\"user_message\":\"Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many beds does the hospital need to handle its daily admissions for one week? Additionally, here are some details: the hospital's admissions office is open seven days during the week. Each daily admission requires one completed intake form before the patient is assigned to a bed.\"},{\"turn\":4,\"user_message\":\"I should also tell you: the hospital has a capacity of 1050 beds.\"},{\"turn\":5,\"user_message\":\"Okay, now can you extend that? Specifically: How many unoccupied beds are in the hospital after 2 weeks? One more thing you should know: One-fifth of the hospital beds are occupied.\"},{\"turn\":6,\"user_message\":\"One more thing — The time period is 2 weeks.\"}],\"public_metadata\":{\"benchmark\":\"Evolving Intent GSM8K\",\"upstream_commit\":\"993d6be9597ac03854b46362ccd647eb1bfd267a\"}}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. The hospital has a capacity of 1000 beds.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital has:\n\n- Total beds: \\(1000\\)\n- Initially occupied beds:  \n  \\[\n  \\frac{1}{5}\\times 1000=200\n  \\]\n- Patients admitted over 2 weeks:  \n  \\[\n  50\\times 7\\times 2=700\n  \\]\n\nThus, occupied beds after 2 weeks:\n\n\\[\n200+700=900\n\\]\n\nUnoccupied beds:\n\n\\[\n1000-900=\\boxed{100}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
